; A module that keeps three declarations to itself, for
; `920-private-declaration.ax`. See that file for what it pins.
;
; Modules sit beside the cases and are told apart by name:
; digit-prefixed is a case and must declare `; expect N`.
;
; Nothing here is `pub` except the two entry points, which is the
; whole point: before privacy existed, every one of these would have
; been DELETED from the program by the file that imported it, and the
; two public bodies below would have failed to find them - reported at
; THIS file's lines, in a program that merely read it.

; A private data type, its constructor, and a private function that
; matches on it. A public body uses all three.
(data Wrap (W Int))

(:: unwrap (-> Wrap Int))
(fn (unwrap w) (match w ((W x) x)))

; A private helper whose name the importing file also defines. If the
; module's own call reaches the importer's definition instead of this
; one, `quad` answers 4 rather than 18.
(:: scale (-> Int Int))
(fn (scale n) (* n 3))

(pub :: quad (-> Int Int))
(pub fn (quad n) (scale (scale n)))

(pub :: roundTrip (-> Int Int))
(pub fn (roundTrip n) (unwrap (W n)))
